<title>USA: Pratt said to plan 1,000 layoffs within yr.</title>
<headline>Pratt said to plan 1,000 layoffs within yr.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jet engine maker Pratt &amp; Whitney, a unit of United Technologies Corp, is planning to lay off 1,000 workers within the next year, an aide to U.S. Senator Christopher Dodd, Democrat of Connecticut, said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;They are expecting about 1,000 workers in total to be laid off over the next year,&quot; Dodd aide Jennifer Greeson told Reuters.</p>
<p>Pratt spokesman Mark Sullivan said the company does not comment on layoffs before they happen. He said the company has about 12,000 employees in Connecticut and 5,000 in Florida.</p>
